# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Vite writes one of these temp files every time it has to transform an ESM
# vite.config.js on the fly (e.g. during `vite dev`/`vite build` in some
# environments) — harmless, but they accumulate fast and have no reason to
# ever be committed.
vite.config.js.timestamp-*.mjs

# Supabase keys — VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is safe to expose client-side by
# design (protected by Row Level Security, see supabase/schema.sql), but
# .env itself still shouldn't be committed since people copy real project
# URLs/keys into it locally and it's easy to forget which is which.
.env
.env.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
